//! ChatGPT-subscription answers through the official Codex CLI's `codex app-server`
//! (newline-delimited JSON-RPC over stdio).
//!
//! Ported from the Electron client (`src/core/codex/*.js`, `response-stream.js`) and checked
//! against the schema generated by `codex app-server generate-json-schema` (codex-cli 0.160.0).
//! The CLI owns credentials: this module never reads, copies or logs them, never forwards auth
//! URLs or raw payloads in errors, and only ever forwards normal assistant text to callers.
//!
//! Restrictions kept from the Node client:
//! - shell-free spawn of a native executable, allowlisted environment, owned empty working
//!   directory (removed non-recursively when the process ends);
//! - every model thread is ephemeral, read-only, network-less, approval-free and uses the
//!   `openai` provider with tools, MCP servers, shell and skills disabled. The `thread/start`
//!   response must confirm those settings or the process is stopped;
//! - every server→client request (approvals, tool calls, elicitation…) is denied;
//! - a client method allowlist, 8 MB line bound, 200k-character answer bound, request timeouts;
//! - instruction sources limited to at most one standard global `AGENTS.md`/`AGENTS.override.md`
//!   under the Codex home reported by `initialize`.

